{
  "id": "characteristic-roots-regimes",
  "title": "Characteristic Roots: Three Regimes of a 2nd-Order ODE",
  "eyebrow": "second-order linear ODEs",
  "language": "en",
  "duration": 82,
  "topic": "Constant-coefficient 2nd-order linear ODE y'' + 2γy' + ω²y = 0. The ansatz y = e^(rt) gives the characteristic polynomial r² + 2γr + ω² = 0. Its discriminant γ² − ω² classifies solutions into three regimes — overdamped (Δ > 0, two real roots), critically damped (Δ = 0, repeated root), underdamped (Δ < 0, complex conjugate roots).",
  "subject_id": "mat2b",
  "chapter_number": 4,
  "prerequisites": [
    "second-order-to-system"
  ],
  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "manimoIntro",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 6.29,
      "narration": "A second-order linear ODE has three kinds of solution. One small number decides which.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "center",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "manimo-enter",
            "content": "Manimo bobs in centre-screen",
            "delay": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "Three regimes. One discriminant.",
            "delay": 0.7,
            "color": "var(--chalk-100)"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ansatzAndCharPoly",
      "start": 6.29,
      "end": 25.83,
      "narration": "Try the ansatz y equals e to the r t. Plug into y double prime plus two gamma y prime plus omega squared y equals zero, and the exponential factors out. What's left is the characteristic polynomial: r squared plus two gamma r plus omega squared equals zero.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "center",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "y'' + 2γ y' + ω² y = 0",
            "delay": 0.3,
            "color": "var(--chalk-200)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "ansatz: y = e^(rt)",
            "delay": 1.4,
            "color": "var(--violet-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "r² + 2γ r + ω² = 0",
            "delay": 3,
            "color": "var(--amber-300)",
            "position": "centre payoff"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "discriminantThreeCases",
      "start": 25.83,
      "end": 42.39,
      "narration": "Solve with the quadratic formula. The roots are minus gamma plus or minus the square root of gamma squared minus omega squared. The thing under the root — the discriminant — decides everything. Positive, zero, or negative gives three completely different solutions.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "center",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "r = −γ ± √(γ² − ω²)",
            "delay": 0.3,
            "color": "var(--chalk-100)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "Δ = γ² − ω²",
            "delay": 1.6,
            "color": "var(--amber-300)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "Δ > 0  two distinct real roots  →  overdamped",
            "delay": 3,
            "color": "var(--teal-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "Δ = 0  one repeated real root  →  critically damped",
            "delay": 4.2,
            "color": "var(--amber-300)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "Δ < 0  complex conjugate roots  →  underdamped",
            "delay": 5.4,
            "color": "var(--rose-400)"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "threeCurves",
      "start": 42.39,
      "end": 58.64,
      "narration": "Visualise each one. Underdamped: oscillating decay, the wave envelope shrinks like e to the minus gamma t. Critically damped: the fastest decay without crossing zero. Overdamped: slow decay, no oscillation at all.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "full",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "graph-axes",
            "content": "t-y axes spanning t ∈ [0, 6], y ∈ [-0.5, 1.2]",
            "delay": 0,
            "color": "var(--chalk-200)"
          },
          {
            "type": "graph-curve",
            "content": "Underdamped curve (rose) — envelope-modulated cosine",
            "delay": 0.4,
            "color": "var(--rose-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "graph-curve",
            "content": "Critically damped curve (amber) — (1 + ω t) e^(-ω t)",
            "delay": 1.4,
            "color": "var(--amber-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "graph-curve",
            "content": "Overdamped curve (teal) — sum of two real exponentials",
            "delay": 2.4,
            "color": "var(--teal-400)"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sweepDamping",
      "start": 58.64,
      "end": 72.57,
      "narration": "Now sweep gamma from zero up past omega. Watch the solution morph through all three regimes — undamped sine wave, then ringing decay, then the critical edge, then the slow droop of overdamping.",
      "visuals": {
